#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/statusphere-tutorial/en.mdx:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this tutorial, you'll build a status-setting app using custom Lexicons and real-time sync.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/statusphere-tutorial/en.mdx:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can find the source code for this tutorial in the [statusphere-example-app](https://github.com/bluesky-social/statusphere-example-app) repository.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/statusphere-tutorial/en.mdx:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial builds on top of the app created in our [OAuth with NextJS Tutorial](/guides/oauth-tutorial). You should have a completed NextJS OAuth app before starting this tutorial. If you want to skip that step, you can clone the completed OAuth app from the [Cookbook](https://github.com/bluesky-social/nextjs-oauth-tutorial/tree/129cf28b4146ae709e0dac43ce20154ab5237559).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/statusphere-tutorial/en.mdx:45
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You should have installed:\n"
"- Node.js 18-22.x\n"
"- Go 1.25+\n"
"- The pnpm package manager\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/statusphere-tutorial/en.mdx:49
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Note>\n"
"This tutorial currently doesn't work on Node 24.x because of a [Request bug](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/90826).\n"
"</Note>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/statusphere-tutorial/en.mdx:55
#, no-wrap
msgid "Begin by adding these atproto libraries to your existing project:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/statusphere-tutorial/en.mdx:59
#, no-wrap
msgid "You should also have our `lex` CLI tool installed globally:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/statusphere-tutorial/en.mdx:67
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Lexicons](/guides/lexicon) define the schema for records in atproto. To create this tutorial, we've already published a new \"Statusphere\" Lexicon to our repository, available at `xyz.statusphere.status`. You can use `lex` to download and build this Lexicon into your project:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/statusphere-tutorial/en.mdx:71
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you want, you can view the downloaded Lexicon file at `lib/lexicons/xyz.statusphere.status.json`. From here, you can run `lex build` to generate TypeScript types for all of your installed Lexicons:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/statusphere-tutorial/en.mdx:77
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Note>\n"
"You could add this command to `package.json` if you needed, but we won't be using it again in this tutorial now that our Lexicons have been built. If you ever add another Lexicon to a project with `lex install`, you'll need to re-run `lex build` with the `--override` flag to regenerate the types.\n"
"</Note>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/statusphere-tutorial/en.mdx:79
#, no-wrap
msgid "One more thing you should do now is update the `SCOPE` constant in `lib/auth/client.ts` to request access to this collection. Atproto permission scopes are Lexicons, so you can add `xyz.statusphere.status` to the list of scopes your app requests:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/statusphere-tutorial/en.mdx:83
#, no-wrap
